    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0183" n="101" xml:id="pg101"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Harvey</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 162.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 27, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 3d of December, No.
                    305, has been received. The proceedings which you took on the occasion of the
                    birth-day of the Emperor of Brazil were proper and commendable.</p>
                <p>This government does not feel serious embarrassment in regard to the affair at
                    Bahia. It reposes confidence enough in the public strength and virtue to insist
                    on its own rights, and to recognize the just rights of other nations.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c. Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
